00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
The Usual Suspects is a 1995 crime thriller film directed by
Bryan Singer and written by Christopher McQuarrie.

13
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:31,000
It stars Kevin Spacey, Gabriel Byrne, Benicio del Toro, Stephen Baldwin,
Kevin Pollak, Chazz Palminteri and Pete Postlethwaite.

14
01:01:50,000 --> 01:01:56,000
The plot follows the interrogation of Roger "Verbal" Kint, a small-time con man, who is one of only
two survivors of a massacre and fire on a ship docked at the Port of Los Angeles.

15
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
Through flashback and narration, Kint tells an interrogator a convoluted story of events that led him and his
criminal companions to the boat, and of a mysterious crime lord—known as Keyser Söze—who controlled them.

16
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:46,000
The film was shot on a $6 million budget and began as a title taken from a column in Spy magazine called "The Usual Suspects", after one of
Claude Rains' most memorable lines in the classic film Casablanca, and Singer thought that it would make a good title for a film.

17
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:11,000
The film was shown out of competition at the 1995 Cannes Film
Festival and then initially released in a few theaters.

18
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
It received favorable reviews and was eventually given a wider release.

19
01:23:55,000 --> 01:24:01,000
Praise went towards the mystery elements, screenplay,
plot twist, and Spacey's performance.

20
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:26,000
McQuarrie won the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay and Spacey won the
Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance.

21
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
The Writers Guild of America ranked the film as having
the 35th-greatest screenplay of all time.

22
01:37:10,000 --> 01:37:16,000
The film explores themes of new york city, robbery, relatives, heist, flashback.

23
01:41:35,000 --> 01:41:41,000
The tone is intense and dark and emotional.
